rtex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"Cliques","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/reductions(into:_:)":{"title":"reductions(into:_:)","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/reductions(into:_:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reductions"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"into"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":", ("},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"